  "goodToKnow": "Die Kavallerie is cavalry, soldiers on horseback; with machine guns and trenches in WWI, it lost its role. Related: der Kavalier, originally a horseman, now a gentleman: Kavalier der alten Schule. Das Kavaliersdelikt is an offence people wrongly treat as trivial: Schwarzfahren ist kein Kavaliersdelikt. From Italian cavallo (horse). Stressed on the last syllable. Plural: die Kavallerien."
